@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] mila-ffi-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover the C ABI validators that write caller-owned
buffers (`mila_route_format`, `mila_trust_document_reconcile`,
`mila_push_key_request_encode` and `mila_session_command_format`): guard bytes
past the declared capacity survive every call, refusals leave the buffer and
`written` untouched, `OutputTooSmall` reports the required length, and every
status stays in the stable set. They also cover agreement of route formatting
with `MilaRoute`, of push key encoding with `mila_push_registration_validate`,
totality of the snapshot, watch-line and command-kind projections with
untouched out-parameters on refusal, the terminal dimension rectangle and
input bounds of the scalar validators, and refusal of stale session and PTY
handles without writing caller storage. JNI exports are not exercised by
properties; they need a JVM and are covered by the Android instrumentation
tests.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture;verification] mila-ffi-single-c-header
`include/mila_ffi.h` MUST be the only C description of the `mila_*` ABI. It is
hand-written, and `tests/header.rs` MUST keep it equal to the crate: exactly
the `#[no_mangle] extern "C"` `mila_*` exports, each with its Rust arity; the
`MilaFfiStatus`, `MilaThreadCommandKind`, `MilaMachineCommandKind` and
`MilaWatchEventKind` enumerators at the Rust discriminants; and every
declaration inside the include guard. Apple's `MilaFFIShim` includes it
through a symlink, never a copy.
